From 2373ee81dfe47367362944d258af21cdead60632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FNGarvin <184324400+FNGarvin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 22:20:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] Fold capture into Save Video/Audio As; name dumps after
 the page title

Save Video/Audio As no longer greys out for MSE/blob-backed media with no
reusable URL -- it now falls back to the same demux-level capture used by
the (now-removed) separate "Dump Media Stream" item. Only truly-nothing-
can-be-done content (DRM with no fallback URL) stays disabled. Unlike a
normal save this doesn't produce a file instantly: it arms capture and the
file is written as playback continues.

Also renamed the aDirPath parameter to aPathPrefix throughout the chain
(WebIDL down to MediaDumpMuxer) to match what it actually is now: dump
filenames are built from a folder path joined with the page's sanitized
title (via the existing getFrameTitle()/DownloadPaths.sanitize() utilities
already used elsewhere in this file), not just a bare directory, so dumps
are identifiable without opening them first.
